/// Shows the Google Ads manager (MCC) and client account tree for a connection, including pending invitations and link status.  ### How the tree is built  It starts from every customer the Google user behind the connection can access directly and walks each tree to any depth with `customer_client`. It then reads each manager's own client links, so every client carries its direct parent, the `managerLinkId` and the link status.  - Invitations a manager sent that the client has not accepted yet appear as clients with `linkStatus: PENDING` (Google returns no name or currency for them). - Refused, canceled and ended links are history and are omitted. - A directly accessible account that is also nested in another tree appears only once, inside that tree.  ### Response fields  - `managerLinks` (on a root): the managers linked to that account, including invitations it can still accept with PATCH /v1/ads/accounts/manager-links. - `directCustomers`: every account the Google user accesses directly (the ones this connection can accept or decline invitations for) with their pending invitations, including accounts that are also nested in a tree. - `unavailable`: customers Google refuses to read (for example a cancelled account), with Google's reason, instead of failing the call. - `truncated`: true when more exist than the limit. Up to 50 roots and 50 managers per root are read. - `cachedAt` and `stale`: the response is cached for 10 minutes per connection.  When the connection is scoped to specific ad accounts, client accounts outside that scope are hidden (managers stay visible).
