/// Bills a Google Ads account to a monthly invoicing payments account of a manager above it, and proposes its account budget, so the account can serve without anyone opening Google Ads.  ### Monthly invoicing only  Google's API cannot add a card or other payment method. So `paymentsAccountId` must be one of the manager's monthly invoicing (consolidated billing) payments accounts listed by GET /v1/ads/accounts/billing.  A manager without monthly invoicing has none, and billing has to be added in Google Ads instead.  ### What it creates  1. A billing setup (Google's BillingSetupService) that starts now on that payments account. 2. An account budget proposal that starts now and never ends: unlimited by default, or capped at `spendingLimit` in the account currency.  Google reviews the budget offline, usually within an hour. Until then the setup reads `APPROVED_HELD` and ads do not serve.  ### Existing billing  This call never replaces existing billing. It is refused with 409 when:  - the customer's current billing setup already has a budget; - the customer is billed to another payments account.  A current setup on the same payments account without a budget (for example after a budget rejection) is reused, so resending the same request finishes it.  ### Retries and validation  Not idempotent and never retried: after a 502 with details.creationStatus=unknown, read GET /v1/ads/accounts/billing before retrying.  Google has no dry run for billing setups. So `validateOnly: true` checks the payments account and the existing billing without creating anything, and asks Google to validate the budget when a setup would be reused.
